      "id": "rx48rsd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO MODAL VERBS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Modal verbs express mood or attitude such as ability, permission, possibility, obligation, and necessity.",
        "Modals are primary auxiliary verbs that are followed directly by the base form of the verb (V1), without 'to' (except for 'ought to' and 'used to').",
        "Modal Perfect structures (Modal + have + V3) represent past action, unfulfilled past action, or past logical deductions.",
        "Semi-modals like 'Need' and 'Dare' act as both main verbs and auxiliary verbs depending on context."
      ],
      "id": "nhcipst"
    },
