      "id": "c18y9t7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "17. HIGH-PROBABILITY SSC RULES"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Never use 'to' after standard modal verbs like can, could, may, might, shall, will, should, must (Incorrect: 'He can to run').",
        "In negative and interrogative structures where 'need' and 'dare' act as modals, do not add '-s' for third-person singular subjects (e.g., 'He need not go', NOT 'He needs not go').",
        "'Should have + V3' denotes an action that ought to have happened in the past but did not, a frequent SSC error-spotting rule."
      ],
      "id": "jjs06h6"
    },
